```java
// Strategy interface
interface DiscountStrategy { double apply(double price); }

// Concrete strategies — each isolated and testable
class NoDiscount      implements DiscountStrategy { public double apply(double p){ return p; } }
class StudentDiscount implements DiscountStrategy { public double apply(double p){ return p * 0.85; } }
class BlackFriday     implements DiscountStrategy { public double apply(double p){ return p * 0.50; } }

// Context: dumb, just delegates
class Cart {
    private final DiscountStrategy discount;
    Cart(DiscountStrategy discount) { this.discount = discount; } // injected
    double checkout(double price) { return discount.apply(price); }
}

// Usage — selection happens OUTSIDE the context
var cart = new Cart(new StudentDiscount());
double finalPrice = cart.checkout(100.0); // 85.0
// New "FestiveDiscount"? Add one class. Cart never changes.
```

*The `if-else` didn't vanish into the context — it became polymorphic dispatch. Selection moves to a factory or DI.*

