```java
interface ShippingStrategy { double calculateCost(double weight, String dest); }

@Component("standard")
class StandardShipping implements ShippingStrategy {
    public double calculateCost(double w, String d) { return w * 5.0; }
}
@Component("express")
class ExpressShipping implements ShippingStrategy {
    public double calculateCost(double w, String d) { return w * 15.0; }
}

// (1) Fixed selection at startup
@Service
class OrderService {
    private final ShippingStrategy shipping;
    OrderService(@Qualifier("express") ShippingStrategy shipping) { this.shipping = shipping; }
    double calc(double w, String d) { return shipping.calculateCost(w, d); }
}

// (2) Dynamic selection at runtime via Map injection
@Service
class FlexibleOrderService {
    private final Map<String, ShippingStrategy> strategies; // {"standard":..., "express":...}
    FlexibleOrderService(Map<String, ShippingStrategy> strategies) { this.strategies = strategies; }
    double calc(String type, double w, String d) {
        return strategies.get(type).calculateCost(w, d); // chosen at runtime
    }
}
```

*Map keys are bean names. With `@Component("express")` the key is `"express"`; with bare `@Component` it defaults to the class name, first letter lowercased.*

